  "observations": [
    "Initial normal library check exited 0 with an unused wrapper warning; redundant caller-constraint cleanup may have raced the check. It is not an immutable execution-source proof.",
    "First source-test build failed only on a private test import; no test or candidate ran. Public qualification replaced that test seam.",
    "Static review moved historical-counter checked_add before all reservations and independently excluded cross-catalog DATA/LVAL/foreign INDEX body claims.",
    "Initial relationship donor passed public read checks but lacked complete TD trailers and candidate-map roles required by the allocating profile. Two API runs each passed 2 and failed 2; expected errors were not changed.",
    "A retained temporary read-only private probe proved complete declarations and missing OrdinaryCandidate claims; its source was archived and registration removed before final checks.",
    "A fixture-authoring run then failed its free-header assertion: the old raw builder leaves free metadata zero. A new wrapper measures and normalizes only permitted metadata; original donor files, ROWs, slots, indexes and relationships remain unchanged.",
    "Qualified relationship source and all 4 final integration functions pass. No writer admission or relationship expectation was weakened."
  ],
